---
// Case study: Planet Fitness, "No One Knows" (spec campaign).
// Copy rewritten from the old fatimarabi.com/project-3.html. Same case pieces as
// Headspace. The hero finishes the campaign line with a new confession every
// few seconds (src/scripts/planet-fitness.ts).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Scribble from '../../components/Scribble.astro';
import CaseHero from '../../components/case/CaseHero.astro';
import CaseText from '../../components/case/CaseText.astro';
import CaseMedia from '../../components/case/CaseMedia.astro';
import NextProject from '../../components/case/NextProject.astro';
import CaseLine from '../../components/case/CaseLine.astro';

import subway from '../../assets/planet-fitness/subway.jpg';
import billboard from '../../assets/planet-fitness/billboard.jpg';
import instagram from '../../assets/planet-fitness/instagram.png';

// Endings for the hero's "No one knows…". The first one is what shows without
// animation. Kept short so they fit in a few lines on phones.
const endings = [
  'you Googled “how to use a treadmill.”',
  'that’s your sleeping shirt.',
  'you’ve driven by 12 times.',
  'you almost failed gym class.',
  'you rehearsed this in the car.',
  'you don’t know what a lat is.',
];
---

<Base
  title="Planet Fitness: No One Knows"
  description="No One Knows: a spec campaign for Planet Fitness that talks to people with gym anxiety instead of people chasing gains. By Fatima Rabi."
>
  <div data-case class="pf">
    <CaseHero roles={['Concept', 'Copywriting', 'Art direction']}>
      <Fragment slot="title">
        <span class="line"
          ><span><Scribble type="underline" draw="load" delay={0.9} color="var(--blue)">No one knows</Scribble></span></span
        >
        <span class="line"
          ><span><span class="endings" data-endings>
            {
              endings.map((e, i) => (
                <span class="ending" data-ending aria-hidden={i > 0 ? 'true' : undefined}>
                  {e}
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </span></span></span
        >
      </Fragment>
      <p>Spec campaign for Planet Fitness</p>
      <button class="hush" type="button" data-endings-toggle hidden>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
          <path class="icon-pause" d="M4 3h3v10H4zM9 3h3v10H9z" />
          <path class="icon-play" d="M5 2.5v11L13.5 8z" />
        </svg>
        <span data-endings-label>Pause the confessions</span>
      </button>
    </CaseHero>

    <!-- The problem -->
    <section class="case-section theme-cream" aria-labelledby="catch-title">
      <div class="container">
        <CaseText eyebrow="The problem" id="catch">
          <Fragment slot="heading">Every gym ad is talking to people who already go to the gym.</Fragment>
          <p>
            Gains. Grind. Before-and-afters with suspiciously good lighting. Fitness marketing loves preaching to the
            already converted.
          </p>
          <p>
            Meanwhile, a lot of people would quite like to get healthier, and would also quite like to never be seen
            doing it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Planet Fitness literally trademarked the Judgement Free Zone®. <strong
              >So skip the six-packs and talk to the nervous ones.</strong
            >
          </p>
        </CaseText>

        <CaseMedia
          class="case-section__media"
          image={subway}
          sharp
          alt="Subway poster on a tiled platform, a train blurring past: a man at a cable machine, in purple. No one knows you almost failed gym class in grade 10. Join the Judgement Free Zone®."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The insight -->
    <section class="case-section insight theme-red" aria-labelledby="insight-title">
      <div class="container">
        <CaseText eyebrow="The insight" id="insight">
          <Fragment slot="heading"
            >Gym anxiety runs on{' '}<span class="fix"
              ><span class="fix__mark" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.6" aria-hidden="true"
                ><span class="fix__add">imaginary</span><svg class="fix__caret" viewBox="0 0 24 18"
                  ><path d="M2.5 16.2 C6 11.5 9.2 6.8 11.6 2.4 C14.2 7 17.4 11.6 21.5 15.6"></path></svg
                ></span
              ><span class="sr-only">imaginary</span>{' '}judgement.</span
            ></Fragment
          >
          <p>
            The barrier usually isn’t fitness. It’s the embarrassing stuff we’re sure is glaringly obvious to everyone
            else: the ancient T-shirt, the machine we can’t work, the fact that we’re new.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Spoiler: nobody’s looking.</strong> They’re all too busy worrying about their own stuff.</p>
        </CaseText>

        <CaseMedia
          class="case-section__media"
          image={billboard}
          sharp
          alt="Roadside billboard: a gym seen from inside a parked car at night. No one knows you’ve driven by 12 times to see how busy it is. Join the Judgement Free Zone®."
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The answer -->
    <section class="case-section theme-cream" aria-labelledby="answer-title">
      <div class="container">
        <CaseText eyebrow="The answer" id="answer">
          <Fragment slot="heading">Three words, endless{' '}<Scribble type="underline">confessions.</Scribble></Fragment>
          <p>
            Every execution opens with <strong>No one knows</strong> and finishes with a tiny, oddly specific secret.
          </p>
          <p>
            Specific is the whole trick. “Don’t worry, everyone starts somewhere” is wallpaper. “That’s your sleeping
            shirt” is being caught, and let off the hook, in the same breath.
          </p>
        </CaseText>

        <dl class="rules">
          <div class="rule" data-reveal>
            <dt class="rule__label">How it talks</dt>
            <dd class="rule__body">
              Wry and knowing. Like helpful intel from a friend who gets it, not a lecture from a trainer who doesn’t.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="rule" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.1">
            <dt class="rule__label">How it looks</dt>
            <dd class="rule__body">
              Unstaged, caught-in-the-moment photos of regular people. Nobody’s flexing in a mirror.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Social: the captions finish the joke -->
    <section class="case-section case-section--tight theme-cream" aria-labelledby="social-title">
      <div class="container">
        <CaseText eyebrow="On your feed" id="social">
          <Fragment slot="heading">The captions do the follow-through.</Fragment>
          <p>
            The post makes the confession. The caption pats you on the back about it: that 2009 T-shirt blends right in
            with all the fake-vintage band tees anyway. Promise.
          </p>
          <CaseMedia
            slot="aside"
            class="social__phones"
            image={instagram}
            cutout
            sharp
            alt="Two Planet Fitness Instagram posts. A man in a locker room holding up a T-shirt: No one knows that’s your sleeping shirt. A woman checking her phone at the gym: No one knows you Googled “how to use a treadmill.” Captions end with: Promise."
            sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 34rem, calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter))"
          />
        </CaseText>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The line -->
    <CaseLine>
      <Fragment slot="title">
          A gym campaign for people who{' '}<Scribble type="underline" color="var(--blue)" delay={0.3}
            >don’t love gyms.</Scribble
          >
      </Fragment>
          Never aggressive, never overwhelming. Just the reassurance that whatever feels obvious about your fitness
          journey, nobody’s actually keeping track. While everyone else fights over the already converted.
      <Fragment slot="note">
        <p class="the-line__note" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.2">
            Spec work: Planet Fitness didn’t ask. (No one knows.)
          </p>
      </Fragment>
    </CaseLine>

    <NextProject slug="planet-fitness" />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .case-section :global(.case-section__media) {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .case-section--tight {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  /* ---------- Hero: one ending at a time ---------- */

  /* All endings sit in the same spot, so the hero is always as tall as the
     longest one and nothing below it jumps when they swap. */
  .endings {
    display: grid;
    width: 100%;
    /* Room for the underline under "No one knows" */
    margin-top: 0.12em;
    max-width: 11em;
  }
  .ending {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    color: var(--blue);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  /* Without animation, only the first ending shows */
  .ending:not(:first-child) {
    visibility: hidden;
  }
  :global(html.js-motion) .endings {
    /* Masks the endings as they slide in and out (room for descenders) */
    clip-path: inset(-0.1em -0.5em -0.25em -0.5em);
  }

  /* "Pause the confessions": only shown when the endings are moving */
  .hush {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5em;
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
    padding: 0.4em 0.9em 0.4em 0.75em;
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 246 232 / 0.5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    transition:
      background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .hush[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .hush:hover,
  .hush:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--cream);
    background: rgb(255 246 232 / 0.1);
  }
  .hush svg {
    width: 0.75rem;
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  .hush .icon-play,
  .hush.is-paused .icon-pause {
    display: none;
  }
  .hush.is-paused .icon-play {
    display: block;
  }

  /* ---------- The insight: "imaginary" written in above the line ---------- */

  .fix {
    position: relative;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* The added word and its caret come in together */
  .fix__mark {
    position: absolute;
    left: -0.13em;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 0;
    color: var(--blue);
  }
  .fix__add {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 100%;
    translate: -50% 0.1em;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.7em;
    line-height: 1;
    rotate: -4deg;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* A hand-drawn proofreader's caret, sitting in the gap before the word */
  .fix__caret {
    position: absolute;
    left: -0.22em;
    bottom: 0.1em;
    width: 0.44em;
    max-width: none; /* the site caps svgs at their parent's width, which is 0 here */
    height: 0.36em;
    overflow: visible;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  /* Room above the line for the added word (the heading wraps on phones, so
     every line gets the extra room, not just the first) */
  .insight :global(.case-text__heading) {
    padding-top: 0.35em;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ---------- The answer: two small rules ---------- */

  .rules {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l) clamp(2rem, 1rem + 5vw, 5rem);
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .rules {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  .rule {
    padding-top: var(--space-m);
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(34 31 32 / 0.2);
  }
  .rule__label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue-deep);
  }
  .rule__body {
    margin: var(--space-s) 0 0;
    max-width: 30rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.1vw, 2.125rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--red);
  }

  /* ---------- Social ---------- */

  .pf :global(.social__phones) {
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* ---------- The line ---------- */


  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hush {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
